{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":167054,"name":"Guido van Rossum","username":"guido","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/guido/{size}/21_2.png","created_at":"2024-05-23T04:49:36.300Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThis is a call for volunteers to serve on the C API Working Group. The WG’s charter was established by \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0731/#members\"\u003ePEP 731\u003c/a\u003e. Our founding member Irit Katriel has indicated she’d like to resign her WG membership. We thank Irit for her contributions to the WG’s work, in particular as editor of \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0733/\"\u003ePEP 733\u003c/a\u003e (“An Evaluation of Python’s Public C API”).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to the \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0731/#operations-and-process\"\u003ePEP\u003c/a\u003e, we (the remaining WG members) are calling for nominations from the core developer community (a term I propose to interpret in the widest sense possible).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe will then decide on Irit’s replacement based upon the available nominations. Self-nominations are all right. You can nominate by replying to this message or via email to any of the remaining WG members. I propose that we allow a week to collect nominations (similar to the length of time new-core-dev votes are open, to give people time to respond).\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2024-05-23T04:49:36.300Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":230,"reads":166,"readers_count":165,"score":1333.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":54015,"topic_slug":"c-api-working-group-vacancy","display_username":"Guido van Rossum","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0733/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 733 – An Evaluation of Python’s Public C API | peps.python.org","clicks":13},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0731/#members","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 731 – C API Working Group Charter | peps.python.org","clicks":12},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0731/#operations-and-process","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 731 – C API Working Group Charter | peps.python.org","clicks":8},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/c-api-working-group-vacancy-again/56167","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"C API Working Group vacancy (again)","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":8}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":10,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/c-api-working-group-vacancy/54015/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":8}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":8,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":167148,"name":"Erlend E. Aasland","username":"erlendaasland","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/erlendaasland/{size}/4378_2.png","created_at":"2024-05-23T13:03:06.544Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eA big thanks to Irit for all her good work with the PEP and the C API WG!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m nominating myself; I’ve reviewed many C API additions, I am a co-maintainer of the \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/python/pythoncapi-compat\"\u003epythoncapi-compat\u003c/a\u003e project, and I have a strong passion for well-designed APIs. I’ve been following the C API WG closely and I would be glad to take Irit’s place.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2024-05-23T13:03:06.544Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":141,"readers_count":140,"score":343.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":54015,"topic_slug":"c-api-working-group-vacancy","display_username":"Erlend E. Aasland","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/python/pythoncapi-compat","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - python/pythoncapi-compat: The pythoncapi-compat project can be used to write a C extension supporting a wide range of Python versions with a single code base.","clicks":13}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":17}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":3632,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/c-api-working-group-vacancy/54015/2","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":17}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":17,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":167198,"name":"Serhiy Storchaka","username":"storchaka","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/storchaka/{size}/217_2.png","created_at":"2024-05-23T16:01:53.207Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI usually hate to participate in various committees, but since I am an active user of the C API and have some experience in the C API development, and participate in some C API discussions in any way, you might consider my candidacy.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2024-05-23T16:01:53.207Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":132,"readers_count":131,"score":316.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":54015,"topic_slug":"c-api-working-group-vacancy","display_username":"Serhiy Storchaka","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":17}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":44,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/c-api-working-group-vacancy/54015/3","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":17}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":17,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":169036,"name":"Guido van Rossum","username":"guido","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/guido/{size}/21_2.png","created_at":"2024-05-30T15:16:34.089Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThe remaining WG members have deliberated, and we’ve selected Erlend. Erlend, welcome to the C API WG! We’ll contact you privately with the gory details. Serhiy: you are a strong candidate, and if we have another vacancy you are our number one pick. (And I say that without irony.)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2024-05-3